## Jaeger previews trace investigations with visible evidence

Source: Jaeger Maintainers · CNCF — https://www.cncf.io/blog/2026/11/10/jaeger-previews-ai-assisted-troubleshooting-and-genai-observability-for-opentelemetry-traces-at-kubecon/
Published: 2026-11-10
Channel: news

Jaeger is an open-source distributed tracing tool that helps engineers follow requests across services. Large traces can bury useful evidence among many spans, each a record of one operation; model calls, retrieval and tool execution add more steps to examine.

First, engineers can ask the experimental Ask Jaeger assistant questions in ordinary language. Its answers stream into the interface alongside visible tool calls. An optional Model Context Protocol endpoint, an interface agents use to call tools, provides focused ways to discover traces, examine errors and inspect individual operations. Rather than send an entire trace to a model, agents retrieve evidence as each investigation step needs it.

Next, specialized views use OpenTelemetry’s shared field conventions to show model interactions, agent activity, token use and tool execution alongside service traces. These capabilities remain an experimental preview. The maintainers invite teams to enable them, follow the integration guide and provide feedback; they do not report a general accuracy benchmark.

Why it matters: For Jaeger operators: test known failures and inspect the evidence behind each answer.

