## Braintrust brings projects and access controls into Terraform review

Source: Braintrust — https://www.braintrust.dev/blog/terraform
Published: 2026-11-10
Channel: news

Braintrust is a platform for observing agent runs and evaluating their outputs. Its Terraform provider manages projects, permissions and credentials as code. As more teams build agents, repeating setup manually makes it harder to maintain consistency while giving each team appropriate access.

First, create an organization and a service token, then supply that token through the BRAINTRUST_API_KEY environment variable. Define the desired resources in Terraform configuration and initialize the provider. Run terraform plan to inspect proposed changes before applying them. Supported resources include groups, roles, service accounts, projects, dataset containers and score definitions. Version control preserves the change history.

For an existing organization, Braintrust’s export utility generates configuration and matching import instructions. Review both together, inspect the plan and import resources into Terraform state without recreating them. The provider reads current settings and translates configuration into API requests. Braintrust recommends this approach for shared settings that change infrequently; dataset contents, logs and experiments remain in application workflows.

Why it matters: For Braintrust platform teams: review permissions in Terraform plans and keep evaluation data in application workflows.

