## Langfuse records prompt-cache outcomes on request traces

Source: Langfuse · GitHub — https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/releases/tag/v4.78.0
Published: 2026-11-10
Channel: github

Langfuse is an AI observability platform that records application traces and evaluation scores. Its stable release adds prompt-cache outcome tags to request spans, records describing individual operations within a trace. This makes the cache outcome part of the evidence attached to a request, rather than leaving reviewers with only the surrounding application activity.

The release also changes what reviewers see when working with evaluation results. First, the add-score menu can show score-configuration details. Next, when invalid stored score rows are filtered, Langfuse issues a warning. The notes describe that warning without quantifying how many records might be affected or claiming that filtered rows are repaired.

For Topics setup, teams can filter the traces used in the setup flow, and non-transient model-test failures are logged. These are selected operational changes from a broader release that also adds an external HTTP code-evaluation dispatcher. The release notes do not describe that dispatcher’s deployment requirements or provide a measured improvement in evaluation accuracy.

Why it matters: For Langfuse operators: inspect known cache outcomes and investigate warnings before treating score views as complete.

